PLAIN ENGLISH SUMMARY (not legally binding)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  FREE:   Any number of people running Meridian locally on their own
          machines. Teams of any size where each person installs and
          runs the software themselves. Connecting local instances to
          a shared hosted database (e.g. Postgres on Neon or Railway)
          for coordination is explicitly free regardless of team size.

          Self-hosting the dashboard and MCP server on your own
          infrastructure for internal use is permitted, provided you
          do not publish deployment instructions, tooling, or guides
          that enable others to do the same.

  PAID:   Offering Meridian or a substantially similar product as a
          hosted service to third parties. Publishing deployment guides,
          Docker images, Helm charts, or any tooling that packages
          Meridian for others to host. Any product that competes
          directly with Meridian's commercial offerings.

  NEVER:  The above Paid uses during the Protection Period, without
          a separate written commercial license.

  LATER:  After the Protection Period, this license converts to
          GPL-3.0. Everything becomes fully copyleft open source.

